<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       id="release-notes" title="Release notes">

    <show-structure for="chapter" depth="2"/>

    <p>
        Every released version, and where its notes are.
    </p>

    <table style="header-row">
        <tr>
            <td>Version</td>
            <td>Released</td>
            <td>Status</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>%version%</td>
            <td>2026-08-31</td>
            <td>Current</td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <chapter title="Where the notes are" id="where">
        <p>
            One file holds them:
            <a href="https://github.com/aether-framework/aether-weaver/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md">CHANGELOG.md</a>.
            The <a href="https://github.com/aether-framework/aether-weaver/releases">GitHub
            release</a> shows the same text. Its workflow reads that section out of the file.
        </p>

        <p>
            An entry names what arrived, what moved, and what broke.
            <a href="artifacts.topic">Artefacts and modules</a> has what each coordinate publishes.
            <a href="install.topic">Install</a> has where the number goes.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="What the number promises" id="semver">
        <deflist>
            <def title="Patch — 0.1.1">
                <p>A fix. Nothing you compiled against moves.</p>
            </def>
            <def title="Minor — 0.2.0">
                <p>Something was added. What you wrote still compiles, and still weaves.</p>
            </def>
            <def title="Major — 1.0.0">
                <p>Something you may have to change. The entry says what to write instead.</p>
            </def>
            <def title="Outside the promise">
                <p><code>de.splatgames.aether.weaver.api.experimental</code>. Every type there
                    carries <code>@ApiStatus.Experimental</code>, and that annotation is the whole
                    promise.</p>
            </def>
        </deflist>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Moving up a version" id="upgrading">
        <p>
            Read the entry's <emphasis>Known limitations</emphasis> first. That half says what the
            version still does not do.
        </p>

        <p>
            Then check the JDK floor, which is %jdk%. The enforcer stops an older build by name,
            rather than failing later on a missing class.
        </p>

        <p>
            These pages ship with the framework. This site was built from the version above, and
            <a href="building-and-testing.topic">Building and testing</a> builds both from a clone.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <seealso>
        <category ref="contributing">
            <a href="repository-layout.topic">Repository layout</a>
            <a href="building-and-testing.topic">Building and testing</a>
        </category>
        <category ref="reference">
            <a href="artifacts.topic">Artefacts and modules</a>
        </category>
    </seealso>
</topic>
